00:23:01.370 --> 00:23:05.310
Nearly half a million people have now fled the fighting in the Syrian city of Aleppo.

00:23:05.450 --> 00:23:09.350
The UN has criticised Russia for not allowing aid into areas of the city

00:23:09.350 --> 00:23:11.630
where people are desperate for food and medical supplies.

00:23:12.190 --> 00:23:13.950
Our correspondent Richard Galpin reports.

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:20.360
Pro-government forces are pushing deeper and deeper

00:23:20.360 --> 00:23:22.720
into rebel-held territory in Aleppo.

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:26.380
Their offensive has momentum,

00:23:27.480 --> 00:23:30.000
and they've now been attacking the southern border,

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:40.350
part of the key rebel enclave. But opposition fighters have been hitting back, desperately

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:44.870
trying to hold on to what remains of their stronghold in the city, which has been in

00:23:44.870 --> 00:23:51.700
their hands for years. The rebel-held area, marked in grey on this map, has already shrunk

00:23:51.700 --> 00:23:57.350
dramatically in recent days, with much of the northern part now in government hands.

00:23:57.350 --> 00:24:00.000
And as the offensive continues, there's speculation

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:06.950
the rebels could be pushed out of the city altogether within weeks.

00:24:06.950 --> 00:24:13.170
The collapse of the rebel front lines under intense bombardment has led to around 30,000

00:24:13.170 --> 00:24:19.850
civilians fleeing, many crossing into government-held areas where they can get food and medicine.

00:24:19.850 --> 00:24:24.870
But the fate of the men arriving here is unknown.

00:24:24.870 --> 00:24:30.000
For those still living inside the rebel enclave, life is increasingly desperate.

00:24:30.320 --> 00:24:36.130
Hundreds of casualties, no medicine, not even anaesthetics for surgery, and very little

00:24:36.130 --> 00:24:38.130
food.

00:24:38.130 --> 00:24:45.580
Today, the United Nations said the total number of people in need of help in Aleppo was overwhelming.

00:24:45.580 --> 00:24:52.340
400,000 internally displaced in Western Aleppo are now joined by tens of thousands or more.

00:24:52.340 --> 00:24:54.210
We need a winter programme for them.

00:24:54.210 --> 00:25:00.000
Europe panicked because we got 400,000 from Syria, all of Europe.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:03.510
West Aleppo has that alone.

00:25:03.510 --> 00:25:07.450
- One possible answer to this crisis now being discussed

00:25:07.450 --> 00:25:10.180
is to create humanitarian corridors

00:25:10.180 --> 00:25:13.470
to allow the sick and injured to leave eastern Aleppo

00:25:13.470 --> 00:25:18.170
and to send in supplies of food and medicine to the area.

00:25:18.170 --> 00:25:22.710
Richard Galpin, BBC News.

